  era: "Section 18 \xB7 Arrival of Europeans \xB7 1498 \u2013 1760s"
  title: Dutch
  text: The Dutch East India Company, founded in 1602, set up trading posts at Masulipatnam, Pulicat and Chinsura and traded in spices and textiles. Defeated by the English at Bedara in 1759, they turned their focus to Indonesia.
